From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 07:11:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: test frame-sequential stereo on DisplayPort

Stream (amdgpu_dm_connector suite):
- a frame-sequential 1920x1080 mode at 120 Hz on a DisplayPort stream gets
  TIMING_3D_FORMAT_INBAND_FA and VIEW_3D_FORMAT_FRAME_SEQUENTIAL and keeps
  its 2D link timing (1920 by 1080 active, 2200 by 1125 total, 297 MHz);
- the same mode on an MST, eDP, DVI or HDMI stream, and a 2D mode or an
  HDMI 3D layout on a DisplayPort stream, get neither;
- mod_build_vsc_infopacket() on the stream of the frame-sequential mode
  builds VSC SDP revision 1 (HB0 00h, HB1 07h, HB2 01h, HB3 01h) with DB0
  0x01, and revision 5 (HB2 05h, HB3 13h) with the same DB0 when VSC
  colorimetry is in use; the 2D mode builds none;
- dm_link_sends_frame_sequential(): a DCN link at HBR2 to a single-stream
  DisplayPort sink sends it; DCE, the MST, eDP, HDMI, DVI and virtual
  signals, no sink, no link, VGA, DVI and HDMI protocol converters, a
  128b/132b link, Panel Replay and a DC without a link service do not;
- dm_connector_can_send_frame_sequential(): DisplayPort connectors of a DCN
  opt in; DCE, MST ports, connectors without a link, eDP, HDMI, DVI and VGA
  connectors do not;
- amdgpu_dm_connector_mode_valid() lets the mode through to stream
  validation on the DCN DisplayPort link and returns MODE_NO_STEREO on DCE,
  MST, eDP and HDMI sinks and behind an HDMI converter.

Plane (amdgpu_dm_plane suite):
- amdgpu_dm_plane_check_frame_sequential() accepts the primary plane
  covering the 3840x1080 frame from a linear XRGB8888 framebuffer, and a
  2560x1440 eye in ARGB16161616F; it refuses an overlay and a cursor plane,
  a plane covering one eye or off the origin, a scaled or rotated plane, a
  tiled framebuffer (GFX9 64K_S_X), NV12, a 1366-pixel eye (5464 bytes, not
  a multiple of 256) and an asynchronous flip; it does not limit planes
  on 2D CRTCs, HDMI 3D layouts, disabled CRTCs or planes without a
  framebuffer;
- amdgpu_dm_plane_atomic_check() refuses a plane without a DC plane state
  (as the cursor is) on a frame-sequential CRTC and accepts it on a 2D one;
- amdgpu_dm_plane_fill_frame_sequential_scaling() and _address() turn the
  plane on a frame-sequential stream into a stereo surface, frame
  alternate, left eye at the framebuffer's address and right eye 7680 bytes
  further, each eye 1920 wide; a 2D stream keeps its graphics address and
  rectangles.

Each of these cases fails when the behaviour it tests is taken out
behind the same functions.

Assisted-by: LLM
